metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://d16r7o1hw8apt"

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Resource_oxam0"]
script = ExtResource("8_hyk2i")
text = "When I first stepped out of the gate, I was escorted to a locked room and spent an hour answering questions for the magistrates. I had to list every shard I had visited in the past ten years, every place I intended to visit while on this shard, and the purpose of every item I brought with me. Eventually they let me go, but that left a bad first impression.

The first thing I noticed was that homes had no ground floor windows. I suppose people really value their privacy here. That was supported by how they speak. No one I talked to would share any details of their life, dodging questions and offering platitudes instead. The only genuine interaction I was able to observe was two kids playing by the river. They took turns dunking each other's head in the water while demanding they confess their crimes, then bursting out laughing.

As I was heading back to the gate, I could swear someone was following me, ducking into alleyways whenever I turned around. But perhaps I was just affected by everyone's paranoia."
gained_argument = ExtResource("12_f6yff")
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://ciddaw1laebi3"

